  "gotchas": [
    {
      "title": "The LED is on the wireless chip",
      "text": "The on-board LED is driven by the CYW43439 wireless chip (WL_GPIO0), not a GPIO, so Pin(25) code from the original Pico does not light it; in MicroPython use machine.Pin('LED').",
      "source": "picow-connect"
    },
    {
      "title": "Some pins are taken by the radio",
      "text": "GPIO23, 24, 25 and 29 are used internally to talk to the wireless chip; GPIO29 also measures VSYS/3.",
